---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  '<p>Administrative staff work in two connected areas: the <strong>administration panel</strong> at <code>/admin</code> (records, resources, and settings) and the <strong>admin workspace</strong> (guided operational screens such as enrollment processing and finance). What you see depends on your role and permissions.</p>\n<h2>Sign-in and security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Sign in with your staff account. Administrators can require <strong>two-factor authentication</strong> (authenticator app or e-mail code) and <strong>passkeys</strong>.</li>\n<li>Use the <strong>school-year and semester selector</strong> in the panel header before entering data, so records land in the correct academic period.</li>\n<li>Press <strong>Ctrl+L</strong> (Windows/Linux) or <strong>⌘L</strong> (macOS) for global search across students, classes, and other records.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Dashboard</h2>\n<p>The panel dashboard summarizes operations with widgets: enrollment, retention, and attrition statistics, demographics, scholarship distribution, clearance status, geographic distribution, recent enrollments and students, resource availability, and upcoming events. Widgets respect the selected academic period and your permissions.</p>\n<h2>Records and resources</h2>\n<p>The sidebar groups the core resources:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Resource</th>\n<th>Typical work</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Students</td>\n<td>Student profiles, documents, signature capture, enrollment checklists, clearances</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Student Enrollments</td>\n<td>Enrollment records, statuses, and history</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Faculties and Accounts</td>\n<td>Teaching staff and user accounts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Courses and Departments</td>\n<td>Programs, curriculum structure, and departments</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Classes and Rooms</td>\n<td>Sections, schedules, capacity, and room assignment</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Events</td>\n<td>School calendar events shown on dashboards</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Schools</td>\n<td>Institutions in a multi-school deployment</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Users and Roles</td>\n<td>Accounts, role assignment, and permission review</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Senior High School</td>\n<td>SHS strands and SHS student records (cluster)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Additional panel pages cover <strong>Timetable</strong> management, <strong>Student Clearances</strong>, <strong>Backups</strong>, and <strong>General Settings</strong>.</p>\n<h2>Developer observability</h2>\n<p>The admin panel sidebar has an <strong>Observability</strong> group linking to the developer tools (each opens in a new tab, only when enabled and permitted): <strong>Laralyze</strong> (<code>/laralyze</code>, <code>developer</code>/<code>super_admin</code>), <strong>Pulse</strong> (<code>/pulse</code>, <code>super_admin</code>), <strong>Telescope</strong> (<code>/telescope</code>, <code>developer</code>), and <strong>Horizon</strong> (<code>/horizon</code>, production images only). See <strong>Core Concepts → Observability</strong> in the docs for roles, enable flags, and 403 troubleshooting. The same group links to <strong>Logs &amp; Retention</strong> (System Settings), where you purge or schedule the cleanup of the data those tools record.</p>\n<h2>Enrollment processing</h2>\n<p>The admin workspace provides the operational enrollment flow:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Search and review applicants.</strong> Look up a student and open their application.</li>\n<li><strong>Verify academically.</strong> The registrar or department head verifies subjects, documents, and assessment.</li>\n<li><strong>Verify payment.</strong> The cashier confirms or records payment.</li>\n<li><strong>Complete or reopen.</strong> Finish the enrollment, or use the authorized undo/reopen action with a reason.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Enrollment reports, analytics, and assessment PDFs are available from the same area. Configuration of availability, eligibility, tuition, and approvals is handled by <strong>Enrollment Blueprints</strong> — see the Blueprint guides in the navigation.</p>\n<h2>Finance</h2>\n<p>The finance area provides dashboards, payment recording, invoices and receipts, and reports. Statements of account can be issued to students and include a signed public verification link. Bulk assessment PDFs are generated in the background; downloads appear when ready.</p>\n<h2>System management</h2>\n<p>The System Management area centralizes institution configuration: school profile and branding, academic periods, grading rules, student identifier formats, deployment mail status, notification templates, analytics, SEO, social sign-in providers, API keys, and the <strong>Feature Toggles</strong> page that switches portal features on or off. SMTP and provider credentials are configured on the server through <code>koakademy configure mail</code>, not in the web application.</p>\n<h3>Logs &amp; retention</h3>\n<p><strong>System Management → Logs &amp; Retention</strong> is the one place to clear diagnostic history and to schedule that clearing. It covers <strong>Pulse</strong>, <strong>Telescope</strong>, <strong>Mail logs</strong>, and <strong>Activity logs</strong> — one card per source.</p>\n<p>Each card shows whether that source is currently recording, how many records are stored, and how many are already older than the saved retention period. From the same card you can:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Prune now</strong> — delete only the records older than the saved retention period.</li>\n<li><strong>Purge all</strong> — delete every deletable record for that source.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Both actions ask you to type the word <code>PRUNE</code> or <code>PURGE</code> before they run, and cleanup is queued, so you can leave the page while it works. The page polls while a cleanup is in progress and lists recent manual and scheduled runs under <strong>Cleanup history</strong>.</p>\n<p>Each source also has its own schedule: a <strong>Scheduled cleanup</strong> switch, how many days of data to keep, whether it runs <strong>daily</strong> or <strong>weekly</strong>, and the <strong>run time</strong> in the app timezone shown at the top of the page. Schedules are read fresh every minute, so saving one takes effect without restarting anything.</p>\n<div class="doc-callout doc-callout-caution">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">Deletion is instance-wide and irreversible</p><p>Cleanup removes logs for <strong>every school</strong> on the instance, not just the school you are looking at. Student, enrollment, and finance records are never touched, and the mail suppression list, Telescope monitored tags, and the cleanup audit trail itself are protected. Deleting a local mail log does not delete anything at your mail provider.</p>\n<p>Export or back up audit history you are required to retain <strong>before</strong> you purge Activity logs.</p>\n</div><h3>Analytics providers</h3>\n<p><strong>System Management → Analytics</strong> controls every third-party analytics script the portal loads. A fresh install sends none.</p>\n<p>You can add as many providers as you need, including several instances of the same provider (for example one Umami site per domain). Each instance is saved as its own entry with its own enable switch, so you can turn one off without touching the others. A master switch above the list disables all of them at once.</p>\n<p>Add a provider with the picker at the top of the page. Its form is generated from the provider&#39;s own definition, so the fields shown always match what that service needs. The available providers are:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Provider</th>\n<th>Hosting</th>\n<th>Notable options</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Umami</td>\n<td>Self-hosted</td>\n<td>Click and scroll heatmaps, session replay (needs v3.2+)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Plausible</td>\n<td>Self-hosted or cloud</td>\n<td>Site domain, API host</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Matomo</td>\n<td>Self-hosted</td>\n<td>Site ID; heatmaps and recording are paid plugins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PostHog</td>\n<td>Self-hosted or cloud</td>\n<td>Autocapture for click maps, rage-click detection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fathom</td>\n<td>Cloud or Fathom Lite</td>\n<td>Lite (self-hosted) or Cloud</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>OpenPanel</td>\n<td>Self-hosted</td>\n<td>Session replay, outgoing-link tracking</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GoatCounter</td>\n<td>Self-hosted</td>\n<td>No cookies, no unique visitor IDs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Countly</td>\n<td>Self-hosted</td>\n<td>Consent requirement toggle</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Counter.dev</td>\n<td>Cloud</td>\n<td>Cookieless, no signup</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cloudflare Web Analytics</td>\n<td>Cloud</td>\n<td>Beacon token from your Cloudflare zone</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Simple Analytics</td>\n<td>Cloud</td>\n<td>Cookie-free</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Google Analytics 4</td>\n<td>Cloud</td>\n<td>GA4 measurement ID</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Microsoft Clarity</td>\n<td>Cloud</td>\n<td>Session recordings and click heatmaps</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>StatCounter</td>\n<td>Cloud</td>\n<td>Project and security code</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Yandex Metrica</td>\n<td>Cloud</td>\n<td>Click map toggle</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Custom Snippet</td>\n<td>Any</td>\n<td>Paste any HTML or script; add as many as you like</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Every entry can be given a name, so two instances of the same provider stay distinguishable, and a <strong>custom snippet override</strong> field lets you replace the generated markup when a service needs something the generator cannot express.</p>\n<div class="doc-callout doc-callout-caution">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">Student data</p><p>Providers marked <em>Hosted</em> send visitor data to a third party, which makes them a data processor for your institution. You have a <code>StudentMedicalRecords</code> module and minors&#39; records in scope, so review your obligations under the Data Privacy Act and your guardian-consent position before enabling Google Analytics, Clarity, or Yandex Metrica. Prefer the self-hosted options.</p>\n<p>Session replay (Umami, OpenPanel, Clarity, Yandex) records what appears on screen, including student names, grades, and medical details. If you enable it, use the strictest masking your provider offers and set a low sample rate.</p>\n</div><div class="doc-callout doc-callout-tip">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">Which one for click and heatmap data?</p><p>Since Umami v3.2, self-hosted Umami gives you click and scroll heatmaps with no third-party processor involved. PostHog&#39;s autocapture is the stronger choice if you want dead-click and rage-click detection as queryable data rather than a visual overlay.</p>\n</div><div class="doc-callout doc-callout-tip">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">Audit trail</p><p>Administrative changes are recorded under <strong>Audit Logs</strong>. When something looks wrong, check there first before changing a record back.</p>\n</div>'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Admin Portal"
  path="/docs/user-guide/admin-portal"
  description="Daily work in the KoAkademy administration panel and admin workspace — records, enrollment, finance, and system management."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
